<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gniezno</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gniezno is a city in Greater <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, western Poland, one of the earliest centres of the Polish state under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piast-dynasty">Piast dynasty</a>. In 1000, at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-gniezno">Congress of Gniezno</a>, Emperor Otto III and Bolesław I founded an archbishopric there, and early kings of Poland were crowned in its cathedral. The archbishop of Gniezno is still the Primate of Poland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gniezno.jpg" alt="Gniezno" width="320" height="197" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diego Delso · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Catedral_de_Gniezno,_Gniezno,_Polonia,_2014-09-20,_DD_40-42_HDR.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
